:: Souvenirs [event sister_quest] {"position":"3650,1775","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "Souvenirs" (sister_souvenirs), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 6.2. Her milestone into corruption stage 1 (Yearning). A week after
   The Ask I show her the photos from the night of the party (Party Animal, $sister.flags.photoTaken): her on her bed under the
   fairy lights, after. She remembers that night only as dreams. I don't threaten her. I call them special memories. She
   feels sick, and then touched that I kept them, and then she asks if she can touch me like that night. Her first
   handjob she'll remember. Afterwards: "Can I do this more often?" No device.
   EXPLICIT blocks: the act itself is left for the author, each block says what happens in it and what's around it. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[1].img>><</silent>>
I text her at eleven: <i>you up? come over for a sec</i>

She's there in under a minute, in the gray hoodie and sleep shorts, with her hair in a lopsided bun and a face mask still drying on her chin that she has clearly forgotten about. She knocks on my open door, which she never does.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "You rang? If this is about a spider, little $sister.callPlayerShort, I'm charging you for it." },
{ who: $player, text: "Close the door for a second, would you?" },
{ text: "She closes it. Something about the way I said it takes the bounce out of her, and she sits down on the end of my bed with her hands tucked into the sleeves." },
{ who: $sister, text: "You're being weird. Is this about the internship? Did I mess something up in the journal?" },
{ who: $player, text: "You didn't mess anything up. I want to show you something. I've been going back and forth for a while on whether I should." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Hand her the phone">>
I open the album and hand her my phone.

She looks at the first photo for a long time without understanding it. It's her room, taken from the doorway, with the fairy lights over the bed and a shape on the bed that's all bare skin and loose hair, one arm thrown over its face.

Then she swipes, and the shape is her.

<<Media "images/characters/sister/events/souvenirs/phone.jpg" 600>>
/* Sister on the end of the bed in the gray hoodie, staring at a phone screen held in both hands, face pale */

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ text: "Her thumb stops, and so does the rest of her. For a few seconds she doesn't breathe at all, and then she does, too fast." },
{ who: $sister, text: "When is this from? When did you..." },
{ who: $player, text: "The night of the party. You came home and you came to find me." },
{ who: $sister, text: "No. No, I dreamed that. I dream about that night all the time, I thought I made it up because I'm a disgusting person and my brain is broken..." },
{ text: "She swipes again, and again, and her hand is shaking now." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Oh my God, it was real. I actually..." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She drops the phone on the comforter like it's hot and presses both sleeves over her mouth. For a second I think she's going to be sick right there on my bed.

<<linkreplace "Wait">>
I don't touch her, and I don't take the phone back. I sit in my desk chair and let her breathe into her sleeves. Part of me wants to go over there and say something soothing, and I'm fairly sure that would ruin it. I want her to get to the bottom of this on her own and look around for something to hold on to, and find me sitting there.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Why do you have these? Why would you keep... are you going to do something with them?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Hey. Look at me for a second." },
{ text: "She does. Her eyes are wet and enormous." },
{ who: $player, text: "Nobody has ever seen them, and nobody ever will. I didn't take them to hurt you." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Then why?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Because that night you told me things nobody has ever said to me, and the next morning you'd forgotten every one of them. I didn't want to be the only one who remembered. To me they're a memory of something special, that's all they are." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

It's close enough to the truth that I almost believe it myself. I watch it reach her in stages: the fear first, then confusion, and then something warm creeping up underneath that she clearly doesn't want there.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "You kept them all this time and never said a word." },
{ who: $sister, text: "You never once made me feel weird about it. I've been feeling weird about it every single day, and you just let me pretend." },
{ who: $player, text: "I didn't think you were ready." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I'm still not ready. I'm wearing a face mask, for God's sake." },
{ text: "She touches her chin, finds the mask, and laughs, horribly, wetly, and starts picking it off in little pieces." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Let her ask">>
She picks the phone back up. She doesn't swipe this time. She just looks at the one on the screen, the one where she's turned toward the camera, half asleep and smiling.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "I remember bits of it. The lights, your belt, and thinking I had to thank you, as if that was the most important thing in the whole world." },
{ who: $sister, text: "And I remember how it felt. Not the drunk part, just being that close to you, and you letting me." },
{ text: "She puts the phone down, face down, very carefully, and looks at her hands instead of at me." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Can I ask you something terrible?" },
{ who: $player, text: "You can ask me anything." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Can I touch you, like that night? Only this time I want to remember it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I don't answer right away. I let her hear herself say it, and sit in it, until her ears go red under the hair.

Then I get up from the chair and sit down next to her on the bed.

<<linkreplace "Let her">>
She's slow about it, and shaky, and completely serious. She pushes the sleeves of the hoodie up to her elbows first, like someone about to wash dishes. She asks if it's okay twice. When she finally opens my jeans her fingers are cold, and she says sorry for that too, and rubs her hands together to warm them, and I almost laugh.

/* EXPLICIT 1, the start. Her hand only, sober, the first time she'll remember. Slow, shaky, very serious about it, the
   way she is about an exam. She looks down at what she's doing a lot, then up at his face to check. She kneels on the
   bed beside him in the hoodie and sleep shorts. He sits still and lets her find her way. The Chat below runs during. */
<<Media "images/characters/sister/events/souvenirs/hj_0.mp4" 600>>
/* Sister kneeling on the bed beside him in the hoodie, sleeves pushed up, looking down, her hand on him */

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Is this right? I can't remember if I was any good at it that night. I was probably terrible, I was drunk." },
{ who: $player, text: "You're doing fine." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Fine. Wow. I'll take fine, I guess." },
{ text: "But she watches my face the whole time, the way she watched it when she read her grades out loud, and every time I breathe a little differently she adjusts, and learns, and gets better. She's always been a fast learner when it's something she cares about." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

There's still one flake of face mask stuck to her chin, right at the edge of her jaw. I reach over and pick it off.

She stares at me. Then she bursts out laughing, helplessly, with her forehead against my shoulder, and whatever was still wound tight in her comes loose all at once.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "I can't believe you let me do this with a face mask on. You let me cry with a face mask on. I'm never going to be cool in front of you again, you know that? That's gone forever." },
{ who: $player, text: "You were never cool in front of me." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Excuse me, I was extremely cool, I was the coolest person in this house for twenty years, ask anyone." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Let her keep going">>
After that she stops talking. Her breathing has changed. She's leaning against my shoulder now, her cheek on my arm, and her free hand has found a fistful of my shirt and is holding on to it.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "I've thought about this so much, every night, and I hated myself every single time. And now it's real, and it's you, and I don't hate any of it." },
{ who: $player, text: "Then don't stop now." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I'm not going to." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

/* EXPLICIT 2, the middle and the finish. More sure of herself now that she's laughed, faster, her forehead against his
   shoulder and her free hand holding a fistful of his shirt. She doesn't look down much anymore, she goes by his
   breathing. When he comes she gasps as if she's the one who did, and doesn't let go. The line below picks up after. */
<<Media "images/characters/sister/events/souvenirs/hj_1.mp4" 600>>
/* Close, faster, her forehead against his shoulder */

Afterwards she stares down at her hand with an expression I can't quite read. Wonder, maybe, like someone who has just watched something hatch.

<<linkreplace "Afterwards">>
She cleans us both up with the tissues on my nightstand, carefully, thoroughly, the way she does everything when it matters to her. Then she sits back on her heels on the bed and looks at me with her hands in her lap.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "That was real. That one counts." },
{ who: $player, text: "And this time you'll remember it." },
{ text: "She nods, slowly. Then she takes a deep breath, and I can see her working up to it, the same way she worked up to asking about the internship." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Could I do that more often?" },
{ text: "She hurries on before I can answer." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Not all the time, I'm not some kind of... I just mean sometimes, when you want. I'd like to be the one who does that for you." },
{ who: $player, text: "Sometimes, then. I'll let you know when." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Okay. Yeah, okay. That's good." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She leaves my phone on the nightstand, face down, without asking me to delete anything. At the door she stops and looks back at it, and then at me, and smiles, a little crooked.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Keep the pictures, by the way. I think I like that you have them." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

Down the hall her door closes, and through the wall I hear her bed creak once as she falls onto it, and then a sound muffled by a pillow. It takes me a moment to place it, because it's the last thing I expected. She's laughing.

